{"title":"Nulligon","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A nulligon is a zero sided shape. As a shape it is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/7/3b777a79f19daf5ed262a89d36871485f63781cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varnothing$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" />\n</p><p>Technically, all round shapes such as a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a> or an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ellipse\" title=\"Ellipse\">ellipse</a> can be considered nulligons\n<i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Nulligon&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018101714\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 10/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 265/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 180/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.415      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    7.415      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22667:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018101714 and revision id 281817. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}